    "cpu_method": "Separate parent/current JVMs, parent first, -Xmx1g, no concurrent assigned tests or native run. Two fixtures of 50000 frozen cells: uniform STONE or unique two-leaf geometry with LED and STONE. Three warmups and 20 measured complete-history builds. Fixture construction is outside timing. Timed interval includes history/edit/key/map construction. Ordered serialized Edit SHA256 and count checked after every build, outside timing. Current-thread allocated bytes are not retained or peak memory. Single ordered comparison; shared-host GC/JIT/interference remains possible.",
    "heap_method": "Separate JVM for each implementation and retained mode. Actual WorldVoxels geometry stays alive with history, with an optional additional COW history copy. One warmup plus three post-GC heap-delta samples per fixture/mode; two System.gc calls and 100 ms pauses per heap reading. Measures combined retained state against a cleaned baseline, not peak memory. Source fixture lists are not retained. First world cell and history count are checked after each sample; copy replay hashes match. Samples run in a method whose locals leave scope before the next baseline. No 20-run full-system memory claim.",
    "decision": "Keep final key reuse after live-world measurements show lower retained estimates both with and without a history copy. Serialized edit hashes match parent. CPU/allocation diagnostics also improved in both fixtures. This does not qualify full placement/save, maximum package admission, a 100 ms main-thread bound, or city support."
  },
